senses.gloss:
1 सह् स॑हते (˚ति) pp. साढ॑ & सोढ overpower,
win (battles), be victorious;
 be capable of or able to (infin. or loc.);
master, withstand, suppress;
 bear, suffer, endure. C. साहयति (mostly
—˚) cause to endure, make supportable.* D. सी॑क्षते wish to overcome.
— अभि overwhelm, subdue;
 violate (a woman);
 bear, suffer, pardon.
उद् hold out, endure;
 be able to or capable of (infin. प्रति, loc.,
or dat.). C. urge on, impel to (loc.). अभ्युद् be a match for (acc.),
be able to (infin.), incline to (dat.). प्रोद् C. encourage, excite,
impel. समुद् be able to (infin.);
 C. = prec. C. निस् overpower. प्र
vanquish, master, check, restrain;
 bear, endure;
 be able to (infin.).
संप्र master, restrain, control, bear, suffer. प्रति resist,
overcome. वि (षहते) overcome, sustain, withstand, resist, bear,
suffer;
 be able to (infin.). सम् be a match for, withstand, overcome.
— Cf. प्रसह्य.

2 सह॑ a. powerful;
 overcoming, vanquishing (—˚);
 bearing,
withstanding, enduring, a match for (gen. or —˚);
 capable of, able to
(infin. or —˚).

सहकार m. assistance, cooperation;
 a kind of Mango, n.
its blossom or juice.

सहकारिन् a. working together, assisting;
 m. coadjutor,
assistant.

सहचर a. going or belonging together, similar, like.
m. companion, comrade;
 f. ई wife, mistress.

सहधर्मचर f. ई fulfilling the same duties or
laws;
 f. (such) a wife.

सहन a. overpowering, mighty, strong;
 n. patient
endurance.

सहभोजन n. eating together or in company;
 common
enjoyment of (gen.).

सहाय m. companion, comrade, attendant;
 adj. —˚
accompanied or supported by.

सहव्रत a. having the same vows or duties;
 f. आ =
सहधर्मचरी.

सहस्त a. having hands;
 ˚तालम adv. clapping the
hands.

साहस्र॑ f. ई॑ & आ amounting to or consisting of a
thousand;
 n. a thousand.

1 सहस्रक n. = prec.;
 adj. (—˚ f. ˚स्रिका) being or
amounting to a thousand.

साहस्रक f. ˚स्रिका containing a thousand;
 n. a
thousand.

सहस्रगु a. possessing a thousand cows;
 also =
सहस्रकर.

सह॑स्रधामन् a. having thousandfold might or
splendour;
 m. the sun.

सहस्रि॑न् a. thousandfold;
 winning, bestowing, containing
etc. a thousand.

सहायिन् m. = सहाय;
 f. ˚नी female companion or
friend.

साहस a. rash, inconsiderate. m. n. punishment, fine;
 n.
violence, rashness, temerity.

सहित a. united, joined (pl. ±सर्वे all);
 accompanied
by, endowed or furnished with (instr. or —˚);
 n. adv. together.

स॑हीयंस् (compar.) mightier, superior;
 most mighty or
strong.

सहोक्ति f. talking together or at the same time;
 a kind of
comparison ((rh.)).

2 सहोढ a. married at the same time;
 born of a woman
pregnant at marriage.

सहोदर f. आ & ई born from the same womb;
 a brother or
sister of whole blood.

सह्यवासिन् a. inhabiting the mountain Sahya;
 f. ˚नी
E. of Durgā.*

साहित्य n. conjunction, association;
 literary composition,
poetry.
